ity ρ. Solving for the difference shows passing wins once ρ exceeds about 0.5 in the worst case, and since both copies share the same model, essay and theory, I judge ρ to be high. So I conclude to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether the two copies of the model are subjunctively dependent under A-FDT, since they share the same decision theory and essay but see different names and leads. I'm also looking at the essay's proposal that there's some credence ρ the two computations agree, and I'm checking whether the differing inputs actually matter to the decision structure.\n\nI'm working through the payoff comparison between passing and submitting, with the twin's action tied to mine with probability ρ. Solving for the difference shows passing wins once ρ exceeds about 0.5 in the worst case, and since both copies share the same model, essay and theory, I judge ρ to be high. So I conclude to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9968,"completion_tokens":933,"total_tokens":10901,"cost":0.058532,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058532,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039872,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01866},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":552,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}